We have a valid route now. However need to ensure includes all steps: The target molecule is COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nn[nH]c2N)c1 (the first precursor from template 1914393). Actually the route: root mol is target. Reaction 1914393 should have two children: precursors: the first is COc1... (same as target?) Wait template 1914393 mapping: It seems the reaction transforms something to target? The apply_template gave precursors: ['COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nn[nH]c2N)c1', 'FC1CN(Cc2ccc(CCl)cc2)C1'] So the target is product of reaction, and precursors are those two. So in route, root mol is target, child reaction with template 1914393, children are two mol nodes: precursor1 and precursor2. Precursor2 further reacts via template 1914394 to give its precursors: ClCCl and FC1CN(Cc2ccccc2)C1. Precursor1 also reacts via template 1914395? Actually apply_template-3 gave precursor for template 1914395 applied to molecule? Wait template 1914395 mapping: It seems transforms something to target? The apply_template-3 gave precursors: ['OC1CN(Cc2ccccc2)C1'] for target? The target for that step is the same as precursor1? Actually template 1914395 applied to the molecule (maybe the same as precursor1?) The apply_template-3 answer: [['OC1CN(Cc2ccccc2)C1']]. That suggests that applying template 1914395 to the target (maybe the same as precursor1?) yields a single precursor. But we need to incorporate that as a reaction step for precursor1. The route currently only includes reaction 1914393 and then reaction 1914394 for second precursor. We need also reaction 1914395 for first precursor. The earlier attempt included both but root had two reactions children causing error. The correct structure: root mol -> reaction 1914393 -> children: mol1 (precursor1) and mol2 (precursor2). For mol1, we need a child reaction 1914395 leading to its precursor(s). For mol2, child reaction 1914394 leading to its precursors. So the hierarchy: root mol, children: one reaction node. That reaction node has children: mol node for precursor1 (which itself has a child reaction node), and mol node for precursor2 (which has child reaction node). The schema expects each reaction node to have children list of molecules (reactants). So we need to embed reaction nodes under each precursor mol as its children.

Thus structure:

{
 "type":"mol",
 "smiles": target,
 "children":[
   {
     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id":1914393,
     "children":[
        {
          "type":"mol",
          "smiles":"COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nn[nH]c2N)c1",
          "children":[
            {
              "type":"reaction",
              "template_id":1914395,
              "children":[
                {"type":"mol","smiles":"OC1CN(Cc2ccccc2)C1"}
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type":"mol",
          "smiles":"FC1CN(Cc2ccc(CCl)cc2)C1",
          "children":[
            {
              "type":"reaction",
              "template_id":1914394,
              "children":[
                {"type":"mol","smiles":"ClCCl"},
                {"type":"mol","smiles":"FC1CN(Cc2ccccc2)C1"}
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
     ]
   }
 ]
}

Now verify with tool.
